# Secrets for local development. Copy to `.env`, which is gitignored.
# Full instructions, including how to create each of these: see setup.md
#
# ── Nuxt Studio, the content editor at /_studio ────────────────────────────
# You need BOTH of the blocks below, not one of them. The OAuth app is how you
# sign in; the token is how Studio commits. Without a CLIENT_ID, /_studio
# returns "404 No authentication provider found" and there is no dev bypass.
#
# REQUIRED — a GitHub OAuth app. github.com/settings/developers
#   Callback URL must be exactly, including the port you actually run on:
#     http://localhost:3000/__nuxt_studio/auth/github
#
#   Note the names. Some docs pages say NUXT_STUDIO_AUTH_GITHUB_*, which the
#   module does not read. These are the ones the module looks for.
STUDIO_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
STUDIO_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# A fine-grained personal access token, for committing. Needs only
# Contents: read and write on this repository.
# github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
STUDIO_GITHUB_TOKEN=
